{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the festival of harvest, the first-fruits of your labors</b> — I do not know why Scripture refers to them with the definite article, for it has not commanded them nor mentioned them until now. It should rather have said, 'And you shall make a festival of harvest, first-fruits of your labors,' as it says in Deuteronomy (Deuteronomy 16:10): 'And you shall make the festival of Shavuot to YHWH your Elohim.' But perhaps, since it said (Exodus 23:14), 'Three times you shall keep festival to Me in the year,' and specified, 'the festival of unleavened bread you shall keep in the month of the spring' (Exodus 23:15) — that you shall keep it to make a festival at the beginning of the spring — it went back and said: and the other you shall keep, that there be a festival of harvest, first-fruits of your labors, and the third you shall keep, that there be a festival of ingathering at the going out of the year.\n\nNow all of them, when he has gathered in all his produce from the field, are to give thanks to Elohim, for He guards the statutes of the heavens and brings forth bread from the earth to satisfy the craving soul, and the hungry soul He fills with good. This is the meaning of 'before the face of Adonai YHWH' — that He is the Master who sustains His servants, and when they receive their portion from before Him, they come before Him to see what He will command them. Now 'before My face' is like 'before.' And by way of truth, it is from פנים (the inner dimensions), and I have already hinted to you the meaning of the פנים in the Decalogue (Ramban on Exodus 20:3). Therefore it says 'Adonai YHWH,' just as it says the second time, 'Adonai YHWH, the Elohim of Israel' (Exodus 34:23), and likewise, 'Behold the ark of the covenant, the Adon of all the earth' (Joshua 13:11), 'from before the Adon the earth trembles' (Psalms 97:5)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The citation of Joshua 13:11 is likely Joshua 3:11 in standard chapter numbering; the text reads 'הארץ' which may be a variant or error for the same verse cited."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:14:51.302395435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}